    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, using demographic data as indicators for stability can raise concerns about unconscious bias and racial profiling. To avoid this, you can consider using funds flow labels or geospatial-specific metrics, such as properties owned by residents versus investors, or density of small businesses versus chain stores. This approach focuses on underlying features of a neighborhood rather than relying on aggregate demographic data.",
      "source": "target",
